     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Apologies, I deleted my post because I found out what I did wrong. <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">The command line version of tree annotator (v1.10.1) does not automatically pick median heights for the MCC tree. It uses &quot;keep&quot; - I&#39;m not sure what that is exactly. Once I specified which type I wanted (using -heights median), the x-axis and the node ages calculated as &quot;<span><code><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\"></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mrsd</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">height_median&quot;</span></code></span>  match up fine. <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Best,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Divya <br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Thu, 10 Jan 2019 at 16:46, Yu, Guangchuang &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gc...@connect.hku.hk</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">without reproducible example, I have no idea of what you mean.<br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Mon, Jan 7, 2019 at 8:28 PM Divya Venkatesh &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">didel...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi all, <br></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m trying to label nodes in a beast mcc tree with their node ages. <br></div><br><div>I&#39;m plotting the tree and x-axis as: </div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">p </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">  ggtree</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">tree</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> mrsd</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;2018-03-13&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> theme_tree2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">()</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span></div></code></div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">p </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> scale_x_continuous</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">breaks</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2004</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2006</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2008</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2010</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2012</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2014</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2016</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2018</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> minor_breaks</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">seq</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2004</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2018</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> limits </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">NA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2024</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span></div></code></div><br></div><div>I use the limits to allow the full long name of the tip to appear in the tree but removing it doesn&#39;t have an effect on the time scale. <br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>And I calculate node ages as:  <br><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">label</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">round</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mrsd</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">height_median</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span></div></code></div>or <br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">label</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">round</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mrsd</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">height</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span></div></code></div><br></div><div><br>However, neither matches with the x-axis time scale that ggtree produces. </div><div>Example, a node labelled 2016.07 appears at a point well before 2016 in the bottom scale. Am I calculating this wrong? </div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>The &quot;node age&quot; in figtree matches with the x-axis time scale but this calculation doesn&#39;t. How exactly does one calculate the age of the node in ggtree?? <br></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve looked at previous questions regarding node age and height, but I still don&#39;t understand how figtree vs ggtree calculates this metric. Any help understanding this would be greatly appreciated! <br></div><br><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div>Divya <br></div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\n1. G Yu, DK Smith, H Zhu, Y Guan, TTY Lam*. ggtree: an R package for visualization and annotation of phylogenetic trees with their covariates and other associated data, Methods in Ecology and Evolution, 2017, 8(1):28-36. doi:10.1111/2041-210X.12628<br>\r\n <br>\r\n2. G Yu*, TTY Lam, H Zhu, Y Guan*. Two methods for mapping and visualizing associated data on phylogeny using ggtree. Molecular Biology and Evolution, 2018, 35(2):3041-3043. doi: 10.1093/molbev/msy194<br>\r\n <br>\r\nHomepage: <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/software/ggtree\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io/software/ggtree&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482355614000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3kGGQMqBzjFe3o2ydBI5SW\">https://guangchuangyu.github.io/software/ggtree</a><br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;ggtree&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bioc-ggtree...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bioc-...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/bioc-ggtree\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups